<title>UK: Brent reported done at 42 cents over Jan paper.</title>
<headline>Brent reported done at 42 cents over Jan paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>One of today's Brent dates was kept by a trader and sold on to another trader at January +42 cents for the cargo loading Dec 18-20, traders said.</p>
<p>Neither the buyer nor the seller were available to comment on the reported deal, which was seven cents higher than previous trades on Monday.</p>
<p>The second cargo nominated into the paper chain on Tuesday was still going around, a trader said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4088</p>
</text>
